<%# Grade books: one card, four rows, a rule between them.

    This has been three shapes. A 256px rail beside the roster (a secondary column used for a
    collection, which Polaris reserves for metadata). Then four separate `.tw-card` link cards across
    the full width - which fixed the width and broke the surface count: with the roster's table card and
    the trading card, one page carried six card surfaces. Card soup, and it was reported as exactly that.

    A card per item is for items that need one - a summary figure, a person, a preview. Four quarters
    with a name and a status are list rows, which is what Polaris's ResourceList, Primer's Box rows and
    Stripe's list sections all are: **one surface, `divide-y` between rows**. design.md's Dividers
    section allows a row separator and nothing else, so this is the only divider shape available here -
    the `divide-x` between grid cells I first reached for is not in that list.

    The original rail was right about all of this and wrong only about its width. What it could not do
    at 256px was carry each quarter's status, which a teacher otherwise discovers by opening all four.

    The pill's wording comes from `grade_book_status_badge`. The enum's own words were printed here and
    on the grade book page, from two separate `tones` hashes - and "Draft" was reported as unreadable
    on that page, where it sits near a Save button. One mapping now, so the list and the page cannot
    disagree about what a state is called. %>

<section aria-labelledby="grade-books-heading">
  <h2 id="grade-books-heading" class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">Grade books</h2>
  <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
    One per quarter. Recording attendance and grades is what pays students their funds to invest.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-3">
    <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: { padded: false } do %>
      <% if grade_books.any? %>
        <ul class="divide-y divide-slate-200">
          <% grade_books.each do |book| %>
            <li>
              <%# The row is the link, so the target is the row rather than a word in it. %>
              <%= link_to classroom_grade_book_path(@classroom, book),
                          class: "flex items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3 transition-colors " \
                                 "hover:bg-slate-50 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 " \
                                 "focus-visible:outline-sitf-primary" do %>
                <span class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-3">
                  <span class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-900"><%= book.quarter.name %></span>
                  <%= grade_book_status_badge(book) %>
                </span>
                <%= lucide_icon("arrow-right", class: "size-4 shrink-0 text-slate-500") %>
              <% end %>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
      <% else %>
        <%= render layout: "components/ui/empty_state",
                   locals: { compact: true,
                             icon: "book-check",
                             title: "No grade books yet",
                             body: "A grade book is created for each quarter of the school year. " \
                                   "Grade books appear here once those quarters have them." } do %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>
